<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">De Beers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1888</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as De Beers Consolidated Mines</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">De Beers is a diamond mining and trading company founded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kimberley">Kimberley</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> in 1888, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-rhodes">Cecil Rhodes</a> merged the mines of the area into De Beers Consolidated Mines with backing from the Rothschilds. For most of the 20th century it controlled the greater part of the world's rough diamond trade. It took its name from the farm of the De Beer brothers, on which one of the first mines was opened.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/de-beers.jpg" alt="De Beers" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Minnaert · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DeBeersBevHills.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
